        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes unbounded memory growth in the Telegram bot-access invalid-entry warning deduplication.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nReplaced the unbounded `Set<string>` with `createDedupeCache({ ttlMs: 0, maxSize: 4096 })`.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo change for gateways handling fewer than 4 096 distinct invalid entries.\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Module-import proof\n\nImports the patched `bot-access.ts` via vitest — triggers module-level `createDedupeCache` initialisation and confirms the public API is intact:\n\n```text\n$ pnpm vitest run --project extension-telegram extensions/telegram/src/bot-access.proof.test.ts\n\n ✓ bot-access.ts createDedupeCache replacement > module imports cleanly\n   — createDedupeCache initialised at module scope,\n     normalizeAllowFrom, resolveTelegramEffectiveDmPolicy, isSenderAllowed all callable\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  1 passed (1)\n   Duration  573ms\n```\n\n### Lint\n\n```text\n$ pnpm oxlint extensions/telegram/src/bot-access.ts\n  (no output — 0 errors)\n```\n\nAI-assisted: built with Codex",
